From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Kevin Turcios <turcioskevinr@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 02:12:53 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] Live: contrast-adaptive sharpening and HyperSwap pixel boost

Sharpening now uses CAS (clamped to the local range, so no halos) instead
of unsharp masking. Pixel boost runs HyperSwap at 512 px by splitting the
crop into four sub-pixel 256 tiles (sharper, ~3x slower). Both are in the
Quality card and saved in profiles.

Applio-Commit: b3d13c472839f63de59b53c64f48f94ab901357d
